WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.771
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.472 align:start position:0% line:0%
Ooh, that was
a long flight.

00:00:06.505 --> 00:00:08.374 align:start position:0% line:0%
17 and a half hour
flight.

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:10.476 align:start position:0%
- I'll tell you it was worth it,
though.
- Definitely worth it.

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:14.347 align:start position:0%
We're on top of the Marina Bay
Sands hotel in Singapore.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start size:59% position:41%
Believe it or not,
we're not just here
on holiday,

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:69% position:31%
we're actually working
very hard.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.252 align:start size:63% position:38%
'Cause it has one
of the highest rates
of lightning strikes

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.287 align:start size:41% position:59%
in the world.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.656 align:start position:0%
And it's currently in November
at the time we're recording
this.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.825 align:start position:0%
Which is the most active month
for lightning strikes.

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start position:0%
It should be a very interesting
subject to film.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:29.495 align:start position:0%
I've never filmed
lightning.

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:32.365 align:start position:0%
It's incredibly fast,
incredibly unpredictable.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:35.201 align:start size:69% position:31%
Also very dangerous.
Which makes you wonder
why we're on the roof.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.236 align:start position:0%
Yeah, well, thankfully,
there's no storm in currently,

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:40.506 align:start position:0%
but why don't we set up
the Phantom in a nice,
safe location

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.341 align:start position:0%
and wait for a storm
to roll in.

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:44.377
- In a bit.
- In a bit.

00:00:46.745 --> 00:00:48.448 align:start size:88% position:13%
Ah!

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.483
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.361 size:84% position:42%
Here we are in a hotel room

00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:04.363 align:start position:0%
looking out
at the Singapore skyline.

00:01:04.396 --> 00:01:07.366 align:start position:0%
Today, we're using
a Phantom v2512.

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:08.601 align:start position:0%
We often use the 2511,

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.437 align:start position:0%
but this has much more
internal memory.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start position:0%
288 gigs.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.308
And we can usually record what,
like four seconds with the--

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.776
- Two seconds.
- Two seconds.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:20.580
This will record almost eight
at 28,500 frames a second,

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.416 size:81% position:41%
but we're gonna be running
this slightly differently
to how we usually shoot.

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:27.487 align:start position:0%
In that, I'm gonna firstly
partition the round
into multiple segments.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.191 line:0%
And I'm also gonna use a feature
called Image Based Auto-Trigger.

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:33.793 align:start position:0% line:0%
What do you know
about it?

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.495 align:start size:44% position:56%
It sounds like

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.163
'cause it's automatically
triggering it

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:38.598
that you're out of a job.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.500 align:start position:0%
( laughs )
Well, sort of.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.767 align:start position:0%
Let me run you
through it.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.770 align:start position:0%
So the first thing
I'm gonna do

00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start position:0%
is we typically only use one
partition in the memory.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:49.909 align:start position:0%
We can record
for the whole thing.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:52.778 align:start position:0%
This capacity allows us
to record for almost
eight seconds.

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:55.882 align:start position:0%
And because of the duration
of a lightning strike
you don't need eight seconds.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.783 align:start position:0%
So essentially
more beneficial

00:01:57.816 --> 00:02:00.920 align:start position:0%
if we say get eight
different partitions.

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:04.290 align:start position:0%
Giving us a round a second
for each capture.

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:08.161 align:start position:0%
So what I've done is
I've set this little area,
this little box.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.929 align:start size:78% position:22%
- See the red box?
- Yeah.

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:12.398 align:start position:0%
And then I can set how often it
checks and the sensitivity

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:15.768 align:start position:0%
of how big the pixel
change has to be

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.403 align:start position:0%
for it to register
a trigger.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:19.305 align:start position:0%
And then I can position this box
wherever,

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:20.840
so I gonna point it in the sky.

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:23.176 align:start position:0%
That way anything down here,
you know, people taking pictures

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.911 align:start position:0%
or anything like that
shouldn't affect it.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.280 align:start position:0%
But if lightning comes down
through the top

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.382 align:start position:0%
it should trigger
the camera,

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.818
automatically save that point
nine seconds into the mag,

00:02:32.851 --> 00:02:34.654 align:start position:0%
and just immediately
go again.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:37.590
So you're saying that if it sees
lightning it'll save it

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:38.791 align:start size:66% position:34%
- for you.
- Yeah.

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start position:0%
And now in theory,
if I change--

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:45.231 align:start position:0%
if I mimic some
lightning here...

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.567 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Yeah.
- What it'd do?

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.736 align:start size:78% position:22%
Immediately triggered
and then stopped
and it's recording again.

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:53.272 align:start size:78% position:22%
It went in a solid circle
and then it started
recording again.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:55.808 align:start position:0%
So it went one and then
when I turned it off
it went another one.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:59.612 align:start position:0%
And you can see now
it's immediately recording
into the mag.

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:01.881 align:start size:72% position:28%
Oh, yeah. So--
'Cause it was so quick.

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:04.250 align:start size:91% position:9%
When you did it
it went two, three like that.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.686 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah.
- It was immediate. Wow.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.487
So this is pretty much
set up now.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.389
So now what we need to do is
wait for it to become nighttime

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:11.857 size:81% position:41%
or wait a lightning strike

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.860 align:start position:0%
and it should capture
and save automatically

00:03:14.893 --> 00:03:16.862 size:84% position:42%
until it's completely full.

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:18.931 align:start position:0%
So now we just wait.

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:20.900 align:start size:78% position:22%
But wait if it does
everything automatically,

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:24.604 align:start size:66% position:34%
should we...
should we just-- Pub?

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.606
- Pub.
- Pub.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.642
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.585 line:0%
( thunder roaring )

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:42.521 line:0%
Go! Go! Go!
My God.

00:03:42.554 --> 00:03:44.290 align:start size:88% position:13%
- ( laughs )
- Watch out, watch out.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.292 align:start position:0%
We're on the wrong side
of the hotel.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.328 align:start position:0%
Gonna miss all
the lightning.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:50.997 size:84% position:58%
My shorts are falling down.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.999 align:start position:0%
Gotta be striking
on the Bay side.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.001 align:start position:0%
The oceans have got nothing
on this end.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.036
( indistinct chatter )

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:00.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
- We're the opposite.
- We were so well set up in
  there.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.508
- Go ahead.
- Ooh, ow!

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:04.544
Sorry.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.619 align:start size:31% position:69%
All right.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:15.621 align:start size:41% position:59%
This is good.

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.657 align:start position:0%
There's no glass
over here.

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.669 line:0%
( thunder roaring )

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:54.027
( lightning crackling )

00:04:55.627 --> 00:04:58.631
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.041 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Oh, wow!
- The whole sky lit.

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:44.009
Throughout the whole ocean.

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:45.811 align:start size:75% position:25%
It just knows
lightning might be there

00:05:45.844 --> 00:05:47.813 align:start size:81% position:19%
and so I can always focus.

00:05:47.846 --> 00:05:49.849
Yeah, it's lightning.

00:06:55.647 --> 00:06:56.983
( laughs )

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:32.919 align:start size:34% position:66% line:0%
Yeah.

00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:49.662
Dan: Oh, wow!

00:09:01.273 --> 00:09:03.276 line:0%
Wow.

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:19.925 align:start position:0%
Well, that was some absolutely
beautiful footage.

00:09:19.958 --> 00:09:21.694 align:start position:0%
I'm so relieved
